{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2yddnxm4xzd2enfwdif35i3xcq7jbdg4i7qakzyghktrqrzfgocq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumerated\nThe whole library is one file (`c_src/src/lib.c`, 140 lines) plus `include/lib.h`. `nm -D` on the C `.so` exports exactly 7 public symbols — no namespace/renaming macros present. All 7 are translated.\n\n## Symbol parity (completion gate)\n`comm` diff of `nm -D` T-symbols between the C `.so` and `target/release/libc_src.so` is **empty in both directions**:\n`apply_multiplier, classify_mode, convert_negative_overflow, convert_time_factor, get_modified_time, hash_time_value, modeselect`\n\n## Bug-for-bug fidelity decisions\n- **`printf` via libc** — declared `extern \"C\" printf` rather than Rust formatting, so `%.2e` (`5.00e+08`, not Rust's `5e8`), `%X` of negative ints, `%ld`, and stdout buffering/interleaving are byte-identical.\n- **double→int UB** — Rust `as` saturates; C on x86-64 emits `cvttsd2si`, which returns `INT_MIN` (`0x80000000`) for out-of-range/NaN. Implemented `double_to_int` to reproduce that, verified against `1e30`, `±inf`, NaN, and the exact ±2³¹ boundaries.\n- **Signed overflow wraps** — `wrapping_mul/add` in `get_modified_time` (int arithmetic *before* widening to `time_t`, so large day counts wrap at 32 bits), `hash_time_value` (`*= 0x1F`, plus `byte << 24` overflowing into the sign bit via `wrapping_shl`), and `apply_multiplier`.\n- **`switch` fall-through** preserved as additive constant chains (level 4 ⇒ +0x249, default ⇒ `0xDEAD`).\n- **Negative `mode_selector`** — C's truncating `%` yields a negative index, so `modes[mode_index]` reads before the array and the following `strcmp` faults. Confirmed the C segfaults (exit 139, no output) for every negative residue; the Rust reproduces the fault deterministically rather than \"fixing\" it.\n- `classify_mode` uses real `strcmp` on the raw pointer, so it matches C for non-NUL-terminated/invalid pointers too.\n\n## Differential testing\nBuilt one driver linked against `libc_src.so` and ran it against both libraries (verified via `ldd` that DT_RUNPATH is overridden by `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, and that the two `.so` files differ by md5):\n- 3786 lines of output covering all 7 functions with edge cases (0, ±1, INT_MIN/MAX, ±inf, NaN, ±2³¹ boundaries, overflow-inducing day counts, 324 `modeselect` input combinations) — **identical**.\n- Crash parity for 5 negative-residue inputs — same exit code 139, same 0 bytes of output.\n- Piped (fully buffered) stdout — identical md5.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":34385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":402,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5dc1cf7-c3f6-420c-8ade-d2aea5a26960","uuid":"58e11220-bbd1-4b06-8851-3f8e08c3fa5e","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:39:34.650Z"}
